From 1304a58fe734234808599024d5b337fca6dd2c29 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrei-Alexandru Bleortu <me@andrei-z.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 03:04:25 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] AP: Generate the Neighbor Report ANQP-element

Wi-Fi Agile Multiband 3.5.1.1 and 4.3.3 require an AP that receives an
ANQP request for the Neighbor Report ANQP-element to answer with the
BSSs it considers candidates, its own BSS included, each with a BSS
Transition Candidate Preference subelement, the most preferred at 255.
hostapd could only return a static anqp_elem=272 value, which cannot
follow the neighbor report database.

Move the candidate list built for BSS Transition Management Query
responses to neighbor_db.c and, unless anqp_elem=272 is configured,
answer the Neighbor Report ANQP-element from it when the neighbor
report database has the own BSS (rrm_neighbor_report=1). With no STA
associated, the preferences come from the database alone. The element
is also listed in the ANQP Capability List then.

Signed-off-by: Andrei-Alexandru Bleortu <me@andrei-z.com>
---
